From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:10:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/30] Typer, Solver: corrections from the reviews of the
 engine and overload designs

premsubst: a premise that bound later usings must be discharged by the witness
its binder refers to when the caller can name that witness (capture);
projections through a coerced witness lose the coercion, as in name resolution;
binders survive the adaptation of methods, initializers and requirements.
premcommit: a requirement that another one mentions is proved by the witness
that resolving it alone gives.
twins: an exploration without any failure is reused under any bound.
headsubst: the equalities that resolve projections are subgoals of the callee's
coercion, so that a failure is diagnosed.
SemanticDump: name bindings show the site of the declaration.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
